-- title:
--   T_ℓ at an avoided prime lies in the image of Ψ
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}(\mathcal O)$, and let $p$ be a prime lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, i.e. a $2$-dimensional $k$-vector space $V$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho.\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)=\overline{\mathbb Q}\simeq_{\mathbb Q}\overline{\mathbb Q}$ to $\mathrm{End}_k(V)$ that is trivial on the elements fixing some finite subextension of $\mathbb Q$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and assume $\bar\rho$ is absolutely irreducible, meaning that after base change to $\overline{k}$ the only invariant submodules are $\bot$ and $\top$. Let $S,S_0$ be finite sets of natural numbers with all elements of $S$ prime, $p\in S$ and $S_0\subseteq S$, and let $N\ge 1$ be such that every prime divisor of $N$ lies in $S$ and in no case in $S_0$; assume the weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ admit an integral structure, i.e. the $\mathbb C$-span of the $\mathbb Z$-submodule generated by the forms all of whose $q$-coefficients are rational integers is everything. Here $\mathbb T^{S_0}=$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) denotes the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_r$ for primes $r\nmid N$, $r\notin S_0$ and $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N$, $q\notin S_0$, and similarly for $S$; enlarging the omitted set shrinks the algebra, so there is an inclusion $\mathbb T^{S}\hookrightarrow\mathbb T^{S_0}$. Let $\theta':\mathbb T^{S_0}\to k$ be a ring homomorphism such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S_0$ and $\ell\ne p$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $\ell$ is a nonunit, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ and acting on the residue field of $P$ by $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho.\rho(\sigma)$ equals $X^2-\theta'(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S_0$, $\ell\in S$ and $\ell\ne p$. Let $\theta:\mathbb T^{S}\to k$ be the composite of the inclusion with $\theta'$, and let $\Psi$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) to [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S₀ 𝒪 θ'`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) (the localisations of the respective base-changed Hecke algebras at the submonoids determined by $\theta$, $\theta'$) which is compatible with the canonical maps $\pi$, in the sense that $\Psi(\pi(t))=\pi'(\iota(t))$ for all $t\in\mathbb T^{S}$. Then there exists $u$ in [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) with $\Psi(u)=\pi'(T_\ell)$.
--
--   This is the statement that $T_\ell$, for a prime $\ell$ omitted from the larger Hecke algebra but good and distinct from $p$, is hit by $\Psi$: combined with surjectivity for the pair $(S,S_0)$ it gives that the localised Hecke algebras away from $S$ and away from $S_0$ agree, the input to the identification of $\mathbb T_\Sigma$ for varying $\Sigma$ in the modularity-lifting argument. It is used by [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.bijective_of_subset_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.bijective_of_subset_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq).
